  "mirrors": [
    {
      "id": "lem-qft-fock-ccr-car",
      "fields": {
        "statement": "Assume Countable Choice [[def-countable-choice]] and let $H$ be a separable\ncomplex Hilbert space, with separability taken in its Hilbert norm topology\nas defined in [[def-separable-space]], and with the second-variable-linear convention of\n[[def-qft-fock-and-test-spaces]]. On $\\mathcal D_{\\rm fin}$ define the bosonic\ncreation and annihilation maps $a^\\dagger(h)$ and $a(h)$ and the fermionic maps\n$c^\\dagger(h)$ and $c(h)$ as in\n[[def-qft-fock-and-test-spaces]]. Write $a_n(h)$ and $a_n^\\dagger(h)$ for\ntheir restrictions to the $n$th bosonic sector. For bosons set\n\n$$D(a(h))=\\{\\Psi\\in\\mathcal F_s(H):\\sum_{n\\ge1}\\|a_n(h)\\Psi_n\\|^2<\\infty\\},\\qquad D(a^\\dagger(h))=\\{\\Psi\\in\\mathcal F_s(H):\\sum_{n\\ge0}\\|a_n^\\dagger(h)\\Psi_n\\|^2<\\infty\\}.$$\n\nThen $\\mathcal F_s(H)$ and $\\mathcal F_a(H)$ are Hilbert spaces,\n$\\mathcal D_{\\rm fin}$ is dense, and it is a graph core for both maximal\nbosonic sector maps. The bosonic operators on their displayed domains are\nclosed and mutually adjoint, and on $\\mathcal D_{\\rm fin}$ satisfy\n\n$$[a(h),a^\\dagger(k)]=\\langle h,k\\rangle_2I,\\qquad [a(h),a(k)]=[a^\\dagger(h),a^\\dagger(k)]=0.$$\n\nThe fermionic $c(h)$ and $c^\\dagger(h)$ extend to bounded operators on the\nwhole Fock space, with norms $\\|h\\|$, and satisfy on the whole space\n\n$$\\{c(h),c^\\dagger(k)\\}=\\langle h,k\\rangle_2I,\\qquad \\{c(h),c(k)\\}=\\{c^\\dagger(h),c^\\dagger(k)\\}=0.$$\n\nThis is a mathematical construction of the two Fock representations; it does\nnot assign particle statistics to a physical species.",
        "deps": [
          "def-qft-fock-and-test-spaces",
          "def-countable-choice",
          "def-orthogonality-and-orthogonal-complement",
          "def-unbounded-linear-operator-domain-and-graph",
          "def-densely-defined-closed-and-closable-operator",
          "def-adjoint-of-a-densely-defined-unbounded-operator",
          "def-symmetric-self-adjoint-and-essentially-self-adjoint",
          "lem-nrqm-composites-hilbert-tensor-construction",
          "lem-nrqm-composites-bounded-tensor-maps",
          "lem-nrqm-composites-permutation-sector-projections",
          "def-separable-space"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "def-qft-fock-and-test-spaces": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-orthogonality-and-orthogonal-complement": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-unbounded-linear-operator-domain-and-graph": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-densely-defined-closed-and-closable-operator": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-adjoint-of-a-densely-defined-unbounded-operator": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-symmetric-self-adjoint-and-essentially-self-adjoint": "mathematical-premise",
          "lem-nrqm-composites-hilbert-tensor-construction": "mathematical-premise",
